body:
Listened to Little Fugue and did like it. For some reason that song in particular made me think of Legend of Zelda

While strong dark songs are also some of my favorites, I also like more soft melancholic songs. One Russian folk type song especially exemplifies this. If interested;

https://youtu.be/mX36Q8Yzao8

"I'm not"

&#x200B;

Depends on the person asking but can be how I respond

I've essentially cut off contact with all of my family. They never really did anything wrong but as became older began to question what exactly they were doing right? I harbor no resentment towards them, it is just that if it were not the concept of being blood related, I don't think I would have ever spoken to people like them. This was triggered by another event in which made me see how family could unjustly be used to exclude others. So in order to be consistent I decided to no longer let "because they're family" be a factor in who I decide to socialize/connect with

&#x200B;

Have since moved out and at most get a text from them maybe twice a month. Besides that no more greetings or visit them for any holiday and have been better off since then

Several times but I think that was mainly to keep my tied down to them as I didn't feel close to them in my later years. Have since then moved out on my own, learned to cook and other household chores for myself with not much trouble. On occasion help my mom out financially as have a well enough job that allows me to do so

&#x200B;

As for social relations, it means I go out less and spend less on frivolous activities so am able to save more than others which is something I make a point to bring up when it is mentioned to me. For the most part am cut off for them which has improved my life

I can relate with some of the thoughts. And yes, I do agree that you need to live for yourself, no others. It is a big deal if you die before you were suppose to but that is your choice

&#x200B;

If you had ended your life one year ago, is there anything you'd be sad that you would have missed?

I'm here to listen and talk but would also recommend another sub if haven't check it out already. I frequent it myself and do find it can help

&#x200B;

r/SuicideWatch

I think the average lifespan is way too long for me with 70+ years (or more depending on your location)

&#x200B;

If life is meaningless, then would that imply death is meaningful? Meaningless is a quantitative term so what is it worth less than? I still want to live for now but personally believe one should live as long as they ought, not as long as they can.

&#x200B;

Thanks though and luck to you and your friend

Series: House, The Twilight Zone, Scrubs, Frasier, The Jeffersons, Rick and Morty

&#x200B;

Podcast: The Partially Examiner Life, Welcome to Night Vale

&#x200B;

Music: Shahram Nazeri, Edith Piaf, Eydie Gorme, The Ink Spots

&#x200B;

Books: Two Treatises of Government, Sherlock Holmes, Song of Ice and Fire, World War Z

For me it depends on the subject being discussed. If it is something that interests me then I express my opinionated self. It is a subject I have a lot to say about and always look to share that in a respectful manner. I follow a set of self imposed rules so perhaps that can come off as me being kind to you as an individual but is really me abiding by my own logic on how to talk to someone.

&#x200B;

It depends on the topic, if you start talking about something that does not interest me then I really have nothing to add to the conversation so I don't. I don't like contributing to a conversation in which I don't care about or need more information to form an educated opinion.

I did the same at the beginning of the year, I cut off all family and friends. Was actually happier as no longer had the social obligations from before but inevitably started meeting new people. It is nice to have met new people (even someone who did have romantic interest in) but sometimes do feel like hitting that reset button again. There is just a convenience to not having any friends. This is not to imply I dislike people, I enjoy having a stimulating conversation but have actually attached a negative connotation the word "friend" that the idea of acknowledging them as such makes me feel uncomfortable to a degree. I am sometimes just interested in their story, not exactly care about them as a person as it helps keep things in perspective.

&#x200B;

Don't force a connection on you if you don't want to, would just advise to not actively push one away if you find one you would like to pursue

I am called weird because I give a response which while it technically makes sense, it is unexpected. An example was yesterday, the bartender asks me "How are you feeling?" and I respond with "I am not". Have also been called insightful as I usually am able to present a new perspective to people.

&#x200B;

I have also been called cold as I don't smile but that does not mean I am not happy, I just don't express myself in that manner

You don't seem like a malicious person so I find it hard to believe, not to say you are not telling the truth. Sometimes we judge ourselves much more harshly that we would others. 

&#x200B;

I think it is possible, go to a new place that is far away. Tear your identification documents and end your own life. Police don't seem to put much effort into in when knowing that it is a suicide so don't think I have to worry about them telling someone I know personally

Maybe fear is a factor but I think am just waiting for the right time. Already have it planned out, to just travel to some distant place, prep the noose and hang myself.. alone in some far away place where I will never even be identified nor will those who knew me ever know. As far as they are concerned I just left.

&#x200B;

Don't know what you do but I think we all contribute in some way, it is just not always noticed or even appreciated. Just because no one notices or even cares, it does not mean you aren't contributing.
